rsync's bundled getaddrinfo (used: the box has none) accepts a numeric
host only under AI_NUMERICHOST and otherwise hands it to gethostbyname.
AMIX's gethostbyname searches /etc/hosts only (truss on the box: it opens
/etc/hosts, no resolver traffic) and fails on a dotted quad, so
rsync://192.0.2.1/ died "getaddrinfo: 192.0.2.1 8871: Unknown server
error" (rc 10) while a name from /etc/hosts worked.  Real getaddrinfo
never looks a numeric address up: try inet_pton first.

--- a/lib/getaddrinfo.c
+++ b/lib/getaddrinfo.c
@@ -302,6 +302,15 @@
 					&hints,
 					res);
 		} else {
+			/* A dotted quad is an address, not a name: AMIX's
+			 * gethostbyname only searches /etc/hosts and fails on
+			 * "192.0.2.1", where real getaddrinfo never asks. */
+			struct in_addr ip;
+			if (inet_pton(AF_INET, node, &ip) > 0)
+				return getaddr_info_single_addr(service,
+						ntohl(ip.s_addr),
+						&hints,
+						res);
 			return getaddr_info_name(node,
 						service,
 						&hints,
